[[Image:Shrine Kumano hayatama01.jpg|thumb|250 px|A view of Kumano Hayatama Taisha]]{{Nihongo|'''Kumano Hayatama Taisha'''|熊野速玉大社}} is a [[Shinto shrine]] located in [[Shingu, Wakayama|Shingu]], [[Wakayama Prefecture]], on the shores of the Kumanogawa in the [[Kii Peninsula]] of [[Japan]]. It is included as part of the Kumano Sanzan in the [[UNESCO]] [[World Heritage]] site "Sacred Sites and Pilgrimage routes in the Kii Mountain Range". The three Kumano Sanzan shrines are the Sōhonsha ("head shrines") of all Kumano Shrines, lie at between 20 to 40&nbsp;km of distance one from the other and are connected by the pilgrimage route known as {{nihongo|"Kumano Sankeimichi"|熊野参詣道}}<ref name="ss"/>.
== Notes= {{Reflist}}
