{{Short description|Shinto shrine in Wakayama Prefecture, Japan}} {{No footnotes|date=October 2023}} {{Infobox religious building | name = {{Nihongo|'''Kumano Hayatama Taisha'''|熊野速玉大社}} | image = Kumanohayatama-taisha10s4s4440.jpg | caption = A view of Kumano Hayatama Taisha | map_type = Japan | map_alt = | coordinates = {{coord|33|43|55.03|N|135|59|1.41|E|region:JP_type:landmark_scale:1500|display=title,inline}} | map_relief = | map_size = | map_caption = | religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]] | type = | deity = | founded_by = | established = | date_destroyed = | location = [[Shingu, Wakayama|Shingu]], [[Wakayama Prefecture]] | website = | architecture_style = | festival = | leadership = }}
[[File:Kumanohayatama-taisha12s5s4200.jpg|thumb|Haiden]] [[File:Kumanohayatama-taisha02s4s4592.jpg|thumb|Suzumon]] {{Nihongo|'''Kumano Hayatama Taisha'''|熊野速玉大社}} is a [[Shinto shrine]] located in [[Shingu, Wakayama|Shingu]], [[Wakayama Prefecture]], on the shores of the Kumanogawa in the [[Kii Peninsula]] of [[Japan]]. It is included as part of the Kumano Sanzan in the [[UNESCO]] [[World Heritage]] site "[[Sacred Sites and Pilgrimage Routes in the Kii Mountain Range]]". The three Kumano Sanzan shrines are the Sōhonsha ("head shrines") of all [[Kumano Shrine|Kumano shrine]]s, lie at between 20 and 40&nbsp;km of distance one from the other and are connected by the pilgrimage route known as {{nihongo|"Kumano Sankeimichi"|熊野参詣道}}.<ref name="ss">Sacred site "Kumano Sanzan"</ref>
==See also== *[[List of National Treasures of Japan (crafts-others)]] *[[List of National Treasures of Japan (sculptures)]] *[[Sacred Nagi Tree of Kumano Hayatama Taisha]]
