{{afc comment|Wikidata entry [[d:Q335618]] Wikidata name: Kumano Hayatama Taisha [[User:Immanuelle|Immanuelle]] ([[User talk:Immanuelle|talk]]) 07:42, 11 June 2025 (UTC)}} {{Short description|Shinto shrine in Wakayama Prefecture, Japan}} {{No footnotes|date=October 2023}} {{Infobox religious building | name = {{Nihongo|'''Kumano Hayatama Taisha'''|熊野速玉大社}} | image = Kumanohayatama-taisha10s4s4440.jpg | caption = A view of Kumano Hayatama Taisha | map_type = Japan | map_alt = | coordinates = {{coord|33|43|55.03|N|135|59|1.41|E|region:JP_type:landmark_scale:1500|display=title,inline}} | map_relief = | map_size = | map_caption = | religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]] | type = | deity = | founded_by = | established = | date_destroyed = | location = [[:en:Shingu, Wakayama|Shingu]], [[:en:Wakayama Prefecture|Wakayama Prefecture]] | website = | architecture_style = | festival = | leadership = }}
[[File:Kumanohayatama-taisha12s5s4200.jpg|thumb|Haiden]] [[File:Kumanohayatama-taisha02s4s4592.jpg|thumb|Suzumon]] {{Nihongo|'''Kumano Hayatama Taisha'''|熊野速玉大社}} is a [[:en:Shinto shrine|Shinto shrine]] located in [[:en:Shingu, Wakayama|Shingu]], [[:en:Wakayama Prefecture|Wakayama Prefecture]], on the shores of the Kumanogawa in the [[Kii Peninsula]] of [[:en:Japan|Japan]]. It is included as part of the Kumano Sanzan in the [[:en:UNESCO|UNESCO]] [[:en:World Heritage|World Heritage]] site "[[:en:Sacred Sites and Pilgrimage Routes in the Kii Mountain Range|Sacred Sites and Pilgrimage Routes in the Kii Mountain Range]]". The three Kumano Sanzan shrines are the Sōhonsha ("head shrines") of all [[Kumano shrine|Kumano shrine]]s, lie at between 20 and 40&nbsp;km of distance one from the other and are connected by the pilgrimage route known as {{nihongo|"Kumano Sankeimichi"|熊野参詣道}}.<ref name="ss">Sacred site "Kumano Sanzan"</ref>
==See also== *[[:en:List of National Treasures of Japan (crafts: others)|List of National Treasures of Japan (crafts: others)]] *[[:en:List of National Treasures of Japan (sculptures)|List of National Treasures of Japan (sculptures)]] *[[:en:Sacred Nagi Tree of Kumano Hayatama Taisha|Sacred Nagi Tree of Kumano Hayatama Taisha]]
